"Easy Pixels for Woocommerce" is the "Easy Pixels" plugin extension to set the tracking codes on WooCommerce.

== Description ==

"Easy Pixels for WooCommerce" is the ["Easy Pixels" plugin](https://wordpress.org/plugins/easy-pixels-by-jevnet/) extension to set the tracking codes on WooCommerce. 

- Google Analytics tracking
- Google Ads tracking
- Microsoft Advertising (Bing) tracking
- Facebook Ads Pixel tracking
- Twitter Ads Pixel tracking
- Google Tag Manager Events

= Enhanced Analytics tracking for WooCommerce =

It tracks standard Enhanced Analytics events in WooCommerce:

- Google Analytics purchase event
- Single product views 
- Product views in listings
- Add to cart events (ajax and no ajax methods)
- Initiate checkout

= Requeriments =

This plugin requires The ["Easy Pixels" plugin](https://wordpress.org/plugins/easy-pixels-by-jevnet/) and ["Woocommerce" plugin](https://wordpress.org/plugins/woocommerce/) .

== Screenshots ==
1. The admin interface
2. Google Ads Section

== Installation ==

1. Upload the plugin files to the `/wp-content/plugins/easy-pixels-ecommerce-extension-by-jevnet` directory, or install the plugin through the WordPress plugins screen directly.
2. Activate the plugin through the 'Plugins' screen in WordPress
3. Go to "Easy Pixels" Menu option and set the codes you will use.


